Files under this directory are copied over the same path in lineage/ by
scripts/prepare-tree.sh at the start of every build (rsync, no delete).

vendor/partner_gms/GmsCore/GmsCore.apk
    microG GmsCore 0.3.16.1.252432 (versionCode 252432033), from
    https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/releases/download/v0.3.16.1.252432/com.google.android.gms-252432033.apk
    sha256 5338d8a1141e8aa5845d64a41a39a666139fbe2e2499eead7b1f2ecd69980ccb, signer verified as microG
    (certificate SHA-256 9bd06727e62796c0130eb6dab39b73157451582cbd138e86c468acc395d14165).
    The APK is not kept in git: scripts/fetch-prebuilts.sh downloads it to this path and checks
    the sha256 and, where apksigner is available, the signer.
    Kept below the pinned 0.3.17.252432 (owner's decisions of 2026-11-06 and 2026-11-08). 0.3.16.1 is
    0.3.16 plus the security fixes of 2026-09-29 (GHSA-rp4p-8x89-jhv5 and others), released the same
    day as 0.3.17. Known issue: microG issue https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/issues/3853 (Aurora
    Store login stuck on first login or fresh install) is reported for both 0.3.16.1 and 0.3.17; the
    fix (commit 342c2801, 2026-10-26) is in no release yet. 0.3.16, which logged in fine, is kept in
    dl/microg-0.3.16/ for a quick return.
    To return to the pinned version: remove the GmsCore entry from scripts/fetch-prebuilts.sh and
    the APK check from scripts/prepare-tree.sh, then delete this file and
    lineage/vendor/partner_gms/GmsCore/GmsCore.apk; vendorsetup.sh then downloads the version
    named in GmsCore/.version_code again.
